# LeakSanitizer suppressions for `make test-gui SAN=1`.
#
# These are process-lifetime caches of the libraries, not leaks of FM:
# they are allocated once, kept until exit and left to the OS.  The total
# is constant (it does not grow with directories, files or windows opened),
# and the same reports appear on builds before any FM change.
#
# A real FM leak still shows up: its stack has an FM function as the
# allocator (e.g. editor_show), not only a library frame.

# fontconfig: font list / pattern cache built at the first text layout
leak:libfontconfig.so

# GTK renderer: glyph / texture caches created on the first frame of a window
leak:gsk_renderer_render
